WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.684
Your next move can teach you something. Meet
Gambit.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.090
Play a real game against Hermes. Make one
move, and Hermes calculates one reply.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:15.362
You can see it working before the move
lands.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.284
Stuck? Ask for a hint. Hermes starts with a
clue, then reveals more only when you

00:00:25.284 --> 00:00:27.596
ask. The answer stays in your chat.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.774
In Coach mode, Hermes explains the move you
just played, using Stockfish analysis.

00:00:37.774 --> 00:00:42.548
Here is the mistake, why it matters, and a
clear way to improve.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:54.035
Normal mode keeps commentary quiet. Hints
and explanations are there when you ask.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.276
Bring your own games. Search Chess dot com
or Lichess, choose the exact match, and

00:01:02.276 --> 00:01:04.035
replay it with your coach.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.778
Follow the original line, or try another
idea. Hermes responds to your move, while

00:01:12.778 --> 00:01:14.841
the original match stays intact.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.116
Today: play, replay, and understand. Next:
turn recurring mistakes into targeted

00:01:25.116 --> 00:01:28.372
practice. That is where Gambit can go.
